Instruction: Restrict button visibility by orgchart group membership
Goal: Only show a specific button to employees who belong to LEAF orgchart group 52. Everyone else should not see it at all (not just disabled — omitted from the rendered page).
Steps:

Locate the button's markup in the relevant Smarty template file for the page.
Wrap the button in a Smarty conditional using $empMembership['groupID'][52]:

smarty<!--{if $empMembership['groupID'][52]}-->
  <button type="button" id="yourButtonId">
    Your Button Label
  </button>
<!--{/if}-->

If nesting inside an existing group check (e.g. the page is already gated by a broader access group), nest the new check inside it so the button only shows for users who pass both conditions:

smarty<!--{if $empMembership['groupID'][SOME_EXISTING_GROUP_ID]}-->
  <!-- existing gated content -->

  <!--{if $empMembership['groupID'][52]}-->
    <button type="button" id="yourButtonId">Your Button Label</button>
  <!--{/if}-->

<!--{/if}-->

Confirm $empMembership is assigned in that page's controller. If the page doesn't already use $empMembership elsewhere, check with whoever owns the backend/template that it's being passed into the Smarty context — otherwise the {if} will silently evaluate false for everyone.
Verify group 52 membership in Orgchart admin — confirm which employees/teams are currently members, and add or remove people as needed.
Test as both a member and non-member of group 52 to confirm:

Member sees the button and it functions normally.
Non-member does not see the button in the rendered HTML at all (check page source, not just visual hiding).



Note: This is server-side template gating (safest — the button never reaches non-members' HTML). Avoid relying solely on client-side hiding (e.g. CSS display:none via JS), since that can be bypassed by anyone inspecting the page.
